                <pb facs="0301" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg285"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On March 17, Brigadier General Weems, United States Representative on the Allied
                    Control Commission for Hungary, addressed to Lieutenant General Vladimir
                    Petrovich Sviridov, Soviet Acting Chairman of the Commission, a communication
                    concerning recent political developments in Hungary. The communication, the text
                    of which was identical to the draft contained in telegram 492, Secdel 1325, March 12, to Moscow, <ref
                        target="#pg279">page 279</ref>, was also transmitted to the Soviet, British,
                    and Hungarian Governments. The text of the communication was released to the
                    press in Washington on March 17; see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, March 30, 1947, page 583.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
